    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d907">

                <pb facs="0813" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/741: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kelley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-11T13:00:00+03:00">October 11, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:29 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1008. Embassy’s 951, September 24, paragraph 1. Embassy obtained possession today
                    of the 3 bomb sights and other secret instruments which were part of the
                    equipment of the 3 United States Army bombers interned in the Ankara airport.
                    Arrangements have been made to obtain the bomb sight and secret instruments in
                    the bomber interned at Arifiye upon the conclusion of the holidays here. As soon
                    as the Embassy has obtained possession of all the instruments I shall forward
                    them by special courier to the appropriate authorities in Lydda.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kelley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
